  <h2>The Problem</h2>
  <p>
    Testosterone, thyroid, cortisol, growth hormone, DHEA — these signaling molecules
    govern energy, mood, body composition, libido, recovery speed, and cognitive sharpness.
    By 50, most men's hormonal output is 50–70% of what it was at 25. Almost nobody is
    testing for it, and almost nobody is doing anything about it.
  </p>
  <p>
    The "low T" framing undersells what's actually happening. Multiple hormonal axes
    degrade simultaneously: thyroid slows metabolic rate, elevated estradiol suppresses
    testosterone signaling, cortisol dysregulation burns out the HPA axis. The brain needs
    all of these in range. When they're not, no amount of willpower compensates.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Muscle pillar of the 4M framework treats hormone optimization as a foundational
    layer — because no training protocol, nutrition plan, or cognitive stack reaches its
    ceiling inside a hormonally depleted system.
  </p>

  <h2>The Insulting Behaviors</h2>
  <p>These are the most common ways men actively suppress their own hormonal function.</p>
  <ul class="insult-list">
    <li>No baseline lab work in the past 2 years — flying blind on your own biology</li>
    <li>Chronic sleep deprivation (under 7 hours) — testosterone is produced during deep sleep</li>
    <li>Chronic alcohol use — alcohol directly suppresses testosterone production</li>
    <li>Excess visceral body fat — fat tissue converts testosterone to estrogen</li>
    <li>Sedentary lifestyle with no resistance training — resistance training is the most reliable natural testosterone driver</li>
    <li>Daily exposure to endocrine disruptors: plastics, fluoride, common pesticide residues in food</li>
    <li>Chronic unmanaged stress — elevated cortisol directly suppresses testosterone synthesis</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="section-eliminate">Eliminate the Insulting Behavior</h2>
  <p>Start with what's suppressing you. Then optimize what remains.</p>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 1 — Get a Full Panel</h3>
      <p>Total T, free T, TSH, free T3/T4, cortisol AM, DHEA-S, estradiol, SHBG. Without data, you are guessing. Order labs before anything else.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 2 — Resistance Training 3x/Week</h3>
      <p>Compound movements — squat, deadlift, press. The most evidence-backed natural testosterone intervention available to you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 3 — 7+ Hours Sleep, Lights Out by 10:30pm</h3>
      <p>Sleep is when testosterone is synthesized. A bad sleep schedule cannot be offset by any supplement protocol.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 4 — Remove Endocrine Disruptors</h3>
      <p>Switch to glass and stainless steel for food and water storage. Filter tap water. Prioritize organic for the Dirty Dozen produce list.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Step 5 — 4M Hormone Consult</h3>
      <p>Schedule through our contracted licensed telemedicine practice. They handle TRT evaluation, peptide protocols, and thyroid management for appropriate candidates.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
